<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's Kandir sees 1996 deficit 3.5 pct of GDP.</title>
<headline>Brazil's Kandir sees 1996 deficit 3.5 pct of GDP.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian Planning Minister Antonio Kandir said Monday he expected the public sector operational deficit to be about 3.5 percent of Gross Domestic Product in 1996, falling to 2.5 percent in 1997.</p>
<p>Kandir told Reuters in an interview that he expected GDP growth in 1996 to be about 3.0 percent and to be above 4.0 percent in 1997.</p>
<p>He said the government was aiming for a primary surplus of 1.5-2.0 percent next year.</p>
</text>
